---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const stack = [
  { name: 'Astro', href: 'https://astro.build' },
  { name: 'Tailwind CSS', href: 'https://tailwindcss.com' },
  { name: 'GitHub Actions', href: 'https://github.com/features/actions' },
  { name: 'Nix', href: 'https://nixos.org' },
];
---

<Base
  title="This website — Bram Vermeulen"
  description="How this portfolio site is built: Astro, Tailwind CSS, a Nix dev shell and automated deploys to GitHub Pages."
>
  <main class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-24">
    <div
      class="hero-glow pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-72"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
    </div>

    <article class="relative flex flex-col gap-10 pt-14">
      <header class="animate flex flex-col gap-3">
        <a
          href="/#projects"
          class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground text-sm transition-colors"
        >
          &larr; Back to projects
        </a>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">This website</h1>
      </header>

      <section
        class="animate flex flex-col gap-3"
        style="animation-delay: 100ms"
      >
        <h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Project Overview</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          This is a static portfolio site, built with the same approach I use
          for all my projects: reproducible builds, declarative tooling, and
          automated deployments.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        class="animate flex flex-col gap-4"
        style="animation-delay: 180ms"
      >
        <h2 class="text-xl font-medium">The Stack</h2>
        <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
          {
            stack.map(({ name, href }) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={href}
                  class="border-border bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:border-primary/40 hover:text-foreground block rounded-full border px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs transition-colors"
                >
                  {name}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          I built the site using Astro, a static-site framework that ships zero
          JavaScript by default. In fact, the dark-mode toggle is the only
          script running on this page. For styling, I used Tailwind CSS with the
          color system defined as HSL design tokens, allowing both light and
          dark themes to share a single palette definition.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        class="animate flex flex-col gap-3"
        style="animation-delay: 260ms"
      >
        <h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Reproducible Development</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          I don't keep a global Node.js installation on my machines. Instead, a
          Nix flake in the repository handles the toolchain. Running <code
            class="bg-muted rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">nix develop</code
          > gives any machine the exact same environment instantly. This follows the
          same philosophy as the rest of my infrastructure: if it isn't defined in
          a text file, it doesn't exist.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        class="animate flex flex-col gap-3"
        style="animation-delay: 340ms"
      >
        <h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Deployment</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Every push to the <code class="bg-muted rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm"
            >main</code
          > branch triggers a GitHub Actions workflow that builds the site and publishes
          it directly to GitHub Pages. There are no servers to manage and no manual
          steps involved. The repository remains the single source of truth.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        class="animate flex flex-col gap-3"
        style="animation-delay: 420ms"
      >
        <h2 class="text-xl font-medium">Source Code</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          You can explore the full source code on <a
            href="https://github.com/BramVermeulen/bramvermeulen.github.io"
            class="link">GitHub</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
